# brandnana — catalog

Crawl a brand's product catalog — PDP images, prices, titles — for lifestyle / product imagery and assortment evidence.

app :brandnana__catalog do
  title       "brandnana — catalog"
  description "Crawl a brand's product catalog — PDP images, prices, titles — for lifestyle / product imagery and assortment evidence."
end

## Common verbs

```bash
brandnana catalog crawl <domain>                         # auto strategy
brandnana catalog crawl <domain> --strategy shopify      # auto|shopify|context-dev|sitemap|llm
brandnana catalog crawl <domain> --max-urls 200          # cap a sitemap crawl
brandnana catalog crawl <domain> --mirror                # mirror images to R2, rewrite URLs
```

`--strategy auto` picks the right crawler; override only when you know the store (`shopify`) or need a `sitemap`/`llm` fallback. `--mirror` is what you want when the images feed a published workbook (stable R2 URLs instead of hot-linking). `--brand-id <uuid>` ties rows to a brand; `--db` sets the sqlite path.

## What "good" looks like

- Use `--mirror` for any catalog imagery that ends up in a deliverable.
- Cap large stores with `--max-urls` so you don't pay to crawl the whole site.

## Common pitfalls

- Hot-linking un-mirrored PDP images into a workbook (they rot / hot-link-block).
- Forcing a `--strategy` when `auto` would have detected the platform.

